config ZMK_LED_STRIP_INDICATOR
    bool "Connection-status indicator LED strip proxy"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_ZMK_LED_STRIP_INDICATOR_ENABLED
    help
      A led_strip proxy that ZMK underglow writes to (chosen zmk,underglow).
      On an endpoint (central or non-split) it overrides one pixel with a color
      for the current USB/BLE endpoint, then forwards to the real strip. On a
      split peripheral it just forwards untouched.

config ZMK_LED_STRIP_INDICATOR_REFRESH_MS
    int "Re-send the last frame every this many ms (0 = never)"
    depends on ZMK_LED_STRIP_INDICATOR
    default 2000
    help
      WS2812 pixels hold their color until new data arrives, so if the strip
      gets glitched (e.g. data-line noise or a supply dip when the radio gets
      busy, such as a split half reconnecting) it stays wrong -- notably while
      underglow is off and nothing else writes to it. Periodically re-send the
      cached frame (with the indicator pixel) so it recovers on its own. A
      refresh is also sent shortly after every BLE connect / disconnect.

config ZMK_LED_STRIP_INDICATOR_TRACE
    bool "Log every frame forwarded to the strip (debug)"
    depends on ZMK_LED_STRIP_INDICATOR
    help
      Log each forward to the real strip: what triggered it (underglow frame or
      endpoint/profile event), the indicator pixel color sent, the endpoint seen
      and the led_strip_update_rgb() result. For chasing an indicator that
      blanks unexpectedly.
